{"task_id": "HumanEval/0", "solution": "```python\nclass FloatListAnalyzer:\n    @staticmethod\n    def has_close_elements(numbers: list[float], threshold: float) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Determines if any two distinct numbers in the list are closer than the threshold.\n        Returns True if such a pair exists, False otherwise.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(numbers, list):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input 'numbers' must be a list.\")\n        if not all(isinstance(n, (int, float)) for n in numbers):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in 'numbers' must be floats or integers.\")\n        if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input 'threshold' must be a float.\")\n        if threshold < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Threshold cannot be negative.\")\n\n        n = len(numbers)\n        if n < 2:\n            return False\n\n        # Sorting enables O(N log N) performance by checking only adjacent elements.\n        sorted_numbers = sorted(numbers)\n\n        # Iterate through adjacent elements to find a difference less than the threshold.\n        for i in range(n - 1):\n            if abs(sorted_numbers[i] - sorted_numbers[i+1]) < threshold:\n                return True\n        return False\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/2", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\nclass NumberTruncator:\n    \"\"\"\n    Provides utility methods for numerical truncation operations.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def truncate_number(number: float) -> float:\n        \"\"\"\n        Extracts the decimal part of a positive floating-point number.\n        Validates input and returns a float between 0.0 (inclusive) and 1.0 (exclusive).\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(number, float):\n            raise ValueError(\"Input must be a floating-point number.\")\n        if number < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Input number must be positive or zero.\")\n\n        integer_part = math.floor(number)\n        decimal_part = number - integer_part\n        return decimal_part\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/2", "solution": "```python\n# src/__init__.py\n# (This file can be empty or contain package-level initialization if needed)\n\n# src/number_utils.py\nimport math\n\ndef truncate_number(number: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates and returns the decimal part of a given positive floating-point number.\n    It raises TypeError for non-numeric input or ValueError for negative input.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(number, (int, float)):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a number (int or float).\")\n    if number < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input number must be positive.\")\n    \n    integer_part = math.floor(number)\n    decimal_part = number - integer_part\n    return decimal_part\n```\n\n```toml\n# pyproject.toml\n[project]\nname = \"number-truncator\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A utility to truncate numbers and return their decimal part.\"\nauthors = [{ name = \"Your Name\", email = \"your.email@example.com\" }]\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.8\"\nkeywords = [\"number\", \"truncate\", \"decimal\", \"utility\"]\nclassifiers = [\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3\",\n    \"License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License\",\n    \"Operating System :: OS Independent\",\n]\n\n[project.optional-dependencies]\ndev = [\"pytest>=7.0\"]\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n```\n\n```markdown\n# README.md\n# Number Truncator Utility\n\nThis project provides a simple Python utility function to extract the decimal part of a positive floating-point number.\n\n## Features\n\n- **`truncate_number(number)`**: Given a positive float or integer, returns its decimal part.\n  - Handles type validation, raising `TypeError` for non-numeric input.\n  - Handles value validation, raising `ValueError` for negative input.\n  - Correctly handles integer inputs (e.g., `3.0` returns `0.0`).\n  - Correctly handles zero input (e.g., `0.0` returns `0.0`).\n\n## Installation\n\n1. Clone the repository:\n   ```bash\n   git clone https://github.com/your-username/number-truncator.git\n   cd number-truncator\n   ```\n\n2. Install the package (ideally in a virtual environment):\n   ```bash\n   pip install .\n   ```\n\n## Usage\n\n```python\nfrom number_truncator.number_utils import truncate_number\n\n# Example usage\nprint(truncate_number(3.5))      # Output: 0.5\nprint(truncate_number(10.123))   # Output: 0.12300000000000001\nprint(truncate_number(0.75))     # Output: 0.75\nprint(truncate_number(3.0))      # Output: 0.0\nprint(truncate_number(0))        # Output: 0.0\n\ntry:\n    truncate_number(-1.5)\nexcept ValueError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\") # Output: Error: Input number must be positive.\n\ntry:\n    truncate_number(\"hello\")\nexcept TypeError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\") # Output: Error: Input must be a number (int or float).\n```\n\n## Development\n\nTo set up the development environment and run tests:\n\n1. Install development dependencies:\n   ```bash\n   pip install \".[dev]\"\n   ```\n\n2. Run tests:\n   ```bash\n   pytest\n   ```\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 number_utils.py     # Contains the truncate_number function.\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 tests/\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 test_number_utils.py # Unit tests for number_utils.py.\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 pyproject.toml          # Project metadata, dependencies, and build configuration.\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 README.md               # Project description and usage instructions.\n```\n\n## License\n\nThis project is licensed under the MIT License.\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/1", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\nclass ParenSeparator:\n    @staticmethod\n    def separate_paren_groups(paren_string: str) -> List[str]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Separates balanced, non-nested parenthesis groups from an input string.\n        Spaces are ignored, and malformed parts are not included.\n        \"\"\"\n        result_groups: List[str] = []\n        current_group: str = \"\"\n        balance: int = 0\n\n        for char in paren_string:\n            if char == ' ':\n                continue\n            \n            current_group += char\n            if char == '(':\n                balance += 1\n            elif char == ')':\n                balance -= 1\n            \n            # If balance drops below zero, the current group is malformed; discard it and reset.\n            if balance < 0:\n                current_group = \"\"\n                balance = 0\n                continue \n\n            # If balance returns to zero, a complete, balanced top-level group is found.\n            if balance == 0 and current_group:\n                result_groups.append(current_group)\n                current_group = \"\"\n        \n        return result_groups\n```"}
