{"task_id": "HumanEval/6", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\nclass ParenthesesParser:\n    @staticmethod\n    def parse_nested_parens(paren_string: str) -> List[int]:\n        \"\"\" Input to this function is a string represented multiple groups for nested parentheses separated by spaces.\n        For each of the group, output the deepest level of nesting of parentheses.\n        E.g. (()()) has maximum two levels of nesting while ((())) has three.\n\n        >>> parse_nested_parens('(()()) ((())) () ((())()())')\n        [2, 3, 1, 3]\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(paren_string, str):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n        if not paren_string.strip():\n            return []\n\n        groups = paren_string.split(' ')\n        results = []\n        for group in groups:\n            results.append(ParenthesesParser._calculate_group_depth(group))\n        return results\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _calculate_group_depth(group: str) -> int:\n        current_depth = 0\n        max_depth = 0\n        for char in group:\n            if char == '(':\n                current_depth += 1\n                max_depth = max(max_depth, current_depth)\n            elif char == ')':\n                current_depth -= 1\n        return max_depth\n\nparse_nested_parens = ParenthesesParser.parse_nested_parens\n```"}
