{"task_id": "HumanEval/30", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\nclass NumberFilterService:\n    \"\"\"\n    A service for filtering lists of numbers.\n    This class provides methods to extract specific subsets from numerical lists.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def get_positive(self, numbers: List[Union[int, float]]) -> List[Union[int, float]]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Returns a new list containing only the positive numbers from the input list.\n        It validates input types and filters elements strictly greater than zero.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(numbers, list):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input 'numbers' must be a list.\")\n\n        positive_numbers = []\n        for number in numbers:\n            if not isinstance(number, (int, float)):\n                raise ValueError(f\"List contains non-numeric element: {number}\")\n            if number > 0:\n                positive_numbers.append(number)\n        return positive_numbers\n```"}
