{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "```python\nSHIFT_AMOUNT = 5\nALPHABET_SIZE = 26\n\ndef _shift_char(char: str, shift: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Helper function to shift a single character.\n    It handles wrapping for lowercase alphabetic characters and returns non-alphabetic characters unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    if 'a' <= char <= 'z':\n        original_pos = ord(char) - ord('a')\n        # The + ALPHABET_SIZE ensures the result of (original_pos + shift) is non-negative\n        # before the modulo, correctly handling negative shifts.\n        new_pos = (original_pos + shift + ALPHABET_SIZE) % ALPHABET_SIZE\n        return chr(new_pos + ord('a'))\n    return char\n\ndef encode_shift(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    returns encoded string by shifting every character by 5 in the alphabet.\n    \"\"\"\n    return \"\".join([_shift_char(ch, SHIFT_AMOUNT) for ch in s])\n\ndef decode_shift(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    takes as input string encoded with encode_shift function. Returns decoded string.\n    \"\"\"\n    return \"\".join([_shift_char(ch, -SHIFT_AMOUNT) for ch in s])\n```"}
