{"task_id": "HumanEval/55", "solution": "```\nsrc/fibonacci/exceptions.py\n```python\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input to Fibonacci calculations.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\n```\n```\nsrc/fibonacci/calculator.py\n```python\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\nclass FibonacciCalculator:\n    \"\"\"Calculates Fibonacci numbers using an iterative approach.\"\"\"\n    def calculate(self, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Returns the n-th Fibonacci number. Raises InvalidInputError for invalid inputs.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 0:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Invalid input: n must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n        if n == 0:\n            return 0\n        elif n == 1:\n            return 1\n        else:\n            a, b = 0, 1\n            for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n                a, b = b, a + b\n            return b\n\n```\n```\nsrc/fibonacci/__init__.py\n```python\n\n```\n```\ntests/__init__.py\n```python\n\n```\n```\ntests/test_calculator.py\n```python\nimport unittest\nfrom src.fibonacci.calculator import FibonacciCalculator\nfrom src.fibonacci.exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\nclass TestFibonacciCalculator(unittest.TestCase):\n    \"\"\"Tests the FibonacciCalculator class for various scenarios.\"\"\"\n    def setUp(self):\n        self.calculator = FibonacciCalculator()\n\n    def test_fib_positive_numbers(self):\n        \"\"\"Ensures correct calculation for positive integer inputs.\"\"\"\n        self.assertEqual(self.calculator.calculate(10), 55)\n        self.assertEqual(self.calculator.calculate(8), 21)\n        self.assertEqual(self.calculator.calculate(2), 1)\n        self.assertEqual(self.calculator.calculate(3), 2)\n\n    def test_fib_zero(self):\n        \"\"\"Verifies that F(0) returns 0.\"\"\"\n        self.assertEqual(self.calculator.calculate(0), 0)\n\n    def test_fib_one(self):\n        \"\"\"Verifies that F(1) returns 1.\"\"\"\n        self.assertEqual(self.calculator.calculate(1), 1)\n\n    def test_fib_invalid_input_type(self):\n        \"\"\"Checks for InvalidInputError on non-integer inputs.\"\"\"\n        with self.assertRaises(InvalidInputError) as cm:\n            self.calculator.calculate(\"abc\")\n        self.assertIn(\"non-negative integer\", str(cm.exception))\n\n        with self.assertRaises(InvalidInputError) as cm:\n            self.calculator.calculate(10.5)\n        self.assertIn(\"non-negative integer\", str(cm.exception))\n\n    def test_fib_negative_input(self):\n        \"\"\"Confirms InvalidInputError for negative integer inputs.\"\"\"\n        with self.assertRaises(InvalidInputError) as cm:\n            self.calculator.calculate(-5)\n        self.assertIn(\"non-negative integer\", str(cm.exception))\n\n```\n```\npyproject.toml\n```toml\n[tool.poetry]\nname = \"fibonacci-calculator\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A simple library to calculate Fibonacci numbers.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\nreadme = \"README.md\"\npackages = [{include = \"fibonacci\", from = \"src\"}]\n\n[tool.poetry.dependencies]\npython = \"^3.9\"\n\n[tool.poetry.group.dev.dependencies]\npytest = \"^7.0\"\nblack = \"^23.0\"\nisort = \"^5.0\"\nflake8 = \"^6.0\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"poetry-core\"]\nbuild-backend = \"poetry.core.masonry.api\"\n\n```\n```\nREADME.md\n```markdown\n# Fibonacci Calculator\n\nA simple Python library to calculate the n-th Fibonacci number.\n\n## Features\n\n- Calculates the n-th Fibonacci number (F(n)).\n- Handles invalid inputs (non-integer or negative `n`) by raising an `InvalidInputError`.\n- Efficient iterative calculation.\n\n## Installation\n\nThis project uses `poetry`.\n\n```bash\n# Clone the repository\ngit clone https://github.com/your-repo/fibonacci-calculator.git\ncd fibonacci-calculator\n\n# Install dependencies\npoetry install\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n```python\nfrom src.fibonacci.calculator import FibonacciCalculator\nfrom src.fibonacci.exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\ncalculator = FibonacciCalculator()\n\ntry:\n    # Calculate F(10)\n    result = calculator.calculate(10)\n    print(f\"F(10) = {result}\")  # Output: F(10) = 55\n\n    # Calculate F(0)\n    result = calculator.calculate(0)\n    print(f\"F(0) = {result}\")  # Output: F(0) = 0\n\n    # Calculate F(1)\n    result = calculator.calculate(1)\n    print(f\"F(1) = {result}\")  # Output: F(1) = 1\n\n    # Attempt with invalid input\n    calculator.calculate(-5)\nexcept InvalidInputError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\") # Output: Error: Invalid input: n must be a non-negative integer.\n```\n\n## Running Tests\n\nTo run the unit tests:\n\n```bash\npoetry run python -m unittest discover tests\n```\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 fibonacci/\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 calculator.py\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 exceptions.py\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 tests/\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 test_calculator.py\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 pyproject.toml\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 README.md\n```"}
