{"task_id": "HumanEval/59", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef _is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number is prime. Optimizes by checking divisors up to its square root.\"\"\"\n    if num < 2:\n        return False\n    # No need to check for even numbers after 2, as they would have been caught.\n    for i in range(2, int(math.sqrt(num)) + 1):\n        if num % i == 0:\n            return False\n    return True\n\ndef largest_prime_factor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Returns the largest prime factor of n. Assumes n > 1 and is not prime for efficiency.\"\"\"\n    largest_factor = 1\n    d = 2\n\n    # Handle factor 2 explicitly to optimize for even numbers.\n    while n % d == 0:\n        largest_factor = d\n        n //= d\n\n    # Iterate for odd factors up to the square root of the remaining n.\n    d = 3\n    while d * d <= n:\n        while n % d == 0:\n            largest_factor = d\n            n //= d\n        d += 2\n\n    # If n is still greater than 1, it must be the largest prime factor itself.\n    if n > 1:\n        largest_factor = n\n\n    return largest_factor\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/61", "solution": "```python\n# src/__init__.py\n# This file initializes the src package.\n```\n```python\n# src/bracketing_checker.py\nclass BracketingChecker:\n    @staticmethod\n    def correct_bracketing(brackets: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if the given string of parentheses is correctly balanced and nested.\n        Returns True if every opening bracket has a corresponding closing bracket.\n        \"\"\"\n        balance = 0\n        for char in brackets:\n            if char == '(':\n                balance += 1\n            elif char == ')':\n                balance -= 1\n            if balance < 0:  # Closing bracket without a corresponding opening one\n                return False\n        return balance == 0  # True if all brackets are matched, False otherwise\n```\n```toml\n# pyproject.toml\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[project]\nname = \"bracket-validator\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A utility to validate the structural correctness of bracket sequences.\"\nauthors = [{ name = \"Your Name\", email = \"your.email@example.com\" }]\nrequires-python = \">=3.8\"\nlicense = { text = \"MIT\" }\nclassifiers = [\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3\",\n    \"License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License\",\n    \"Operating System :: OS Independent\",\n]\n```"}
