{"task_id": "HumanEval/91", "solution": "```python\n# File: src/boredom_counter/sentence_splitter.py\nclass SentenceSplitter:\n    \"\"\"Utility for splitting text into sentences based on predefined delimiters.\"\"\"\n    SENTENCE_DELIMITERS = ['.', '?', '!']\n\n    def split(self, text: str) -> list[str]:\n        \"\"\"Splits the input text into a list of sentences, handling various delimiters.\"\"\"\n        if not text:\n            return []\n\n        temp_text = text\n        for delimiter in self.SENTENCE_DELIMITERS:\n            temp_text = temp_text.replace(delimiter, delimiter + '###SENTENCE_END###')\n\n        sentences = [\n            s.strip() for s in temp_text.split('###SENTENCE_END###') if s.strip()\n        ]\n        return sentences\n\n```\n```python\n# File: src/boredom_counter/counter.py\nfrom .sentence_splitter import SentenceSplitter\n\nclass BoredomCounter:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates logic for identifying and counting \"boredom\" sentences.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, sentence_splitter: SentenceSplitter = None):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the counter with an optional SentenceSplitter instance.\"\"\"\n        self._sentence_splitter = sentence_splitter if sentence_splitter else SentenceSplitter()\n\n    def count(self, text: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Counts the number of sentences starting with \"I\" in the provided text.\"\"\"\n        sentences = self._sentence_splitter.split(text)\n        boredom_count = 0\n        for sentence in sentences:\n            if self._is_bored_sentence(sentence):\n                boredom_count += 1\n        return boredom_count\n\n    def _is_bored_sentence(self, sentence: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a single sentence starts with \"I\" (case-sensitive and as a whole word).\"\"\"\n        cleaned_sentence = sentence.lstrip()\n        return cleaned_sentence.startswith(\"I \") or cleaned_sentence == \"I\"\n\ndef is_bored(S: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Public entry point to count \"boredom\" sentences in an input string.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(S, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n    if not S:\n        return 0\n    \n    counter = BoredomCounter()\n    return counter.count(S)\n```"}
