{"task_id": "HumanEval/91", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\nclass BoredomCounter:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts \"boredoms\" in text. A boredom is a sentence starting with \"I\".\n    \"\"\"\n    SENTENCE_DELIMITERS = r'[.?!]'\n\n    def is_bored(self, text: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Counts sentences starting with \"I\" in the input text.\n        Raises TypeError if input is not a string.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(text, str):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n        boredom_count = 0\n        sentences = self._split_into_sentences(text)\n        for sentence in sentences:\n            if self._starts_with_i(sentence):\n                boredom_count += 1\n        return boredom_count\n\n    def _split_into_sentences(self, text: str) -> list[str]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Splits the text into a list of cleaned sentences using defined delimiters.\n        Empty strings from splitting are filtered out.\n        \"\"\"\n        raw_sentences = re.split(self.SENTENCE_DELIMITERS, text)\n        sentences = [s.strip() for s in raw_sentences if s.strip()]\n        return sentences\n\n    def _starts_with_i(self, sentence: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if a sentence starts with the exact word \"I\" (case-sensitive).\n        This includes sentences that are just \"I\".\n        \"\"\"\n        return sentence.startswith(\"I \") or sentence == \"I\"\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/92", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Any\n\ndef any_int(x: Any, y: Any, z: Any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if three inputs are integers and if one is the sum of the other two.\n    Returns True if both conditions are met, False otherwise.\"\"\"\n    \n    if not all(isinstance(arg, int) for arg in [x, y, z]):\n        return False\n\n    return (x == y + z) or (y == x + z) or (z == x + y)\n```"}
