{"task_id": "HumanEval/101", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\nclass StringUtils:\n    @staticmethod\n    def words_string(s: str) -> list[str]:\n        \"\"\"Splits a string into a list of words, using commas and spaces as delimiters.\n        Raises TypeError if the input `s` is not a string.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(s, str):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n        words = re.split(r'[, ]+', s)\n        return [word.strip() for word in words if word.strip()]\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/101", "solution": "```python\nimport re\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef words_string(s: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits a string by commas or spaces into a list of words.\n    Each word is stripped of leading/trailing whitespace, and empty words are discarded.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Use regular expression to split by one or more commas or spaces.\n    # Then strip each word and filter out any resulting empty strings.\n    words = re.split(r'[, ]+', s)\n    return [word.strip() for word in words if word.strip()]\n```"}
