{"task_id": "HumanEval/120", "solution": "```python\n# src/max_k_finder/__init__.py\n\"\"\"Package for finding the top k maximum numbers.\"\"\"\n\n# src/max_k_finder/exceptions.py\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input parameters.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\n# src/max_k_finder/finder.py\nimport heapq\nfrom typing import List\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\nclass MaxKFinderService:\n    \"\"\"Service to find the k largest numbers in an array.\"\"\"\n    MIN_ARRAY_LEN = 1\n    MAX_ARRAY_LEN = 1000\n    MIN_ELEMENT_VAL = -1000\n    MAX_ELEMENT_VAL = 1000\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _validate_inputs(arr: List[int], k: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates input array and k against defined constraints.\"\"\"\n        arr_len = len(arr)\n        if not (MaxKFinderService.MIN_ARRAY_LEN <= arr_len <= MaxKFinderService.MAX_ARRAY_LEN):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\n                f\"Array length must be between {MaxKFinderService.MIN_ARRAY_LEN} and {MaxKFinderService.MAX_ARRAY_LEN}, got {arr_len}.\"\n            )\n        if not (0 <= k <= arr_len):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\n                f\"k must be between 0 and array length ({arr_len}), got {k}.\"\n            )\n        for element in arr:\n            if not (MaxKFinderService.MIN_ELEMENT_VAL <= element <= MaxKFinderService.MAX_ELEMENT_VAL):\n                raise InvalidInputError(\n                    f\"Array elements must be between {MaxKFinderService.MIN_ELEMENT_VAL} and {MaxKFinderService.MAX_ELEMENT_VAL}, got {element}.\"\n                )\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def maximum(arr: List[int], k: int) -> List[int]:\n        \"\"\"Returns a sorted list of the k largest numbers from arr.\"\"\"\n        MaxKFinderService._validate_inputs(arr, k)\n\n        if k == 0:\n            return []\n\n        min_heap = [] # A min-heap tracks the k largest elements found.\n        for num in arr:\n            if len(min_heap) < k:\n                heapq.heappush(min_heap, num)\n            elif num > min_heap[0]:\n                heapq.heapreplace(min_heap, num)\n        \n        return sorted(min_heap) # Sort the elements from the heap in ascending order.\n```"}
