{"task_id": "HumanEval/134", "solution": "```python\nclass StringChecker:\n    @staticmethod\n    def check_if_last_char_is_a_letter(txt: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Returns True if the last character of a given string is an alphabetical character\n        and is not a part of a word, and False otherwise.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not txt:\n            return False\n\n        last_char = txt[-1]\n\n        if not last_char.isalpha():\n            return False\n\n        # If it's a single character string, it's considered a word.\n        if len(txt) == 1:\n            return False\n\n        # Check if the character before the last one is a space.\n        second_last_char = txt[-2]\n        return second_last_char.isspace()\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/135", "solution": "```python\nclass CanArrangeService:\n    def can_arrange(self, arr: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Finds the largest index where an element is less than its preceding element.\n        Returns -1 if the array is sorted or has fewer than two elements.\n        \"\"\"\n        n = len(arr)\n        if n < 2:\n            return -1\n\n        # Iterate from right to left, comparing arr[i] with arr[i-1].\n        for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n            if arr[i] < arr[i-1]:\n                return i\n        \n        # If no disorder is found, the array is sorted.\n        return -1\n\n```"}
