{"task_id": "HumanEval/136", "solution": "class IntegerAnalyzer:\n    @staticmethod\n    def largest_smallest_integers(lst: list[int]) -> tuple[int | None, int | None]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the largest negative and smallest positive integers from the input list.\n        Returns a tuple (largest_negative, smallest_positive), with None if not found.\n        \"\"\"\n        negatives = [x for x in lst if x < 0]\n        positives = [x for x in lst if x > 0]\n\n        largest_negative = max(negatives) if negatives else None\n        smallest_positive = min(positives) if positives else None\n\n        return (largest_negative, smallest_positive)"}
