{"task_id": "HumanEval/138", "solution": "```python\n# File: pyproject.toml\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[project]\nname = \"sum-even-checker\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A utility to determine if an integer can be represented as the sum of exactly four positive even numbers.\"\nauthors = [\n    { name=\"Your Name\", email=\"your.email@example.com\" },\n]\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.8\"\nlicense = { text = \"MIT\" }\nkeywords = [\"utility\", \"math\", \"even numbers\"]\n\n[project.urls]\nHomepage = \"https://github.com/yourusername/sum-even-checker\"\nIssues = \"https://github.com/yourusername/sum-even-checker/issues\"\n\n```\n# File: README.md\n# Sum Even Checker\n\nA Python utility to determine if a given integer can be represented as the sum of exactly four positive even numbers.\n\n## Features\n\n- Checks if `n` can be expressed as `e1 + e2 + e3 + e4` where `e` are positive even numbers.\n- Handles non-integer inputs with `TypeError`.\n- O(1) time complexity.\n\n## Installation\n\nThis project is intended to be used as a module. Clone the repository:\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/yourusername/sum-even-checker.git\ncd sum-even-checker\n```\n\nNo further installation steps are typically needed if you're integrating it into another Python project.\n\n## Usage\n\nYou can use the `is_equal_to_sum_even` function directly in your Python code.\n\n```python\nfrom src.sum_even_checker.checker import is_equal_to_sum_even\n\n# Valid cases\nprint(f\"Is 8 a sum of 4 positive even numbers? {is_equal_to_sum_even(8)}\")   # Expected: True\nprint(f\"Is 10 a sum of 4 positive even numbers? {is_equal_to_sum_even(10)}\") # Expected: True\nprint(f\"Is 100 a sum of 4 positive even numbers? {is_equal_to_sum_even(100)}\") # Expected: True\n\n# Invalid cases\nprint(f\"Is 7 a sum of 4 positive even numbers? {is_equal_to_sum_even(7)}\")   # Expected: False (odd)\nprint(f\"Is 6 a s