{"task_id": "HumanEval/150", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Any\n\nclass PrimalityChecker:\n    @staticmethod\n    def _is_prime_optimized(n: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Implements the core primality test logic using optimized trial division.\"\"\"\n        # Handles edge cases and checks divisibility by 2, 3, and then numbers of the form 6k +/- 1.\n        if n <= 1:\n            return False\n        if n <= 3:\n            return True\n        if n % 2 == 0 or n % 3 == 0:\n            return False\n        i = 5\n        while i * i <= n:\n            if n % i == 0 or n % (i + 2) == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 6\n        return True\n\n    def is_prime(self, n: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if the given integer n is a prime number, including input validation.\"\"\"\n        # Raises TypeError for non-integer input and ValueError for negative integers.\n        if not isinstance(n, int):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n        if n < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer for primality test.\")\n        return self._is_prime_optimized(n)\n\n    def x_or_y(self, n: int, x: Any, y: Any) -> Any:\n        \"\"\"Returns x if n is prime, otherwise returns y.\"\"\"\n        # Calls the internal is_prime method to make the primality determination.\n        if self.is_prime(n):\n            return x\n        else:\n            return y\n```"}
