{"task_id": "HumanEval/150", "solution": "```python\n# file: src/__init__.py\n\n\n# file: src/prime_checker.py\nimport math\n\nclass PrimeChecker:\n    \"\"\"Provides functionality to check if a number is prime.\"\"\"\n    def is_prime(self, n: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if an integer n is a prime number.\n        Raises TypeError if n is not an integer.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(n, int):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n\n        if n <= 1:\n            return False\n        if n <= 3:\n            return True\n        if n % 2 == 0 or n % 3 == 0:\n            return False\n\n        i = 5\n        while i * i <= n:\n            if n % i == 0 or n % (i + 2) == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 6\n        return True\n\n# file: src/x_or_y_service.py\nfrom typing import Any\nfrom src.prime_checker import PrimeChecker\n\nclass XOrYService:\n    \"\"\"Service to return x or y based on the primality of n.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, prime_checker: PrimeChecker):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the service with a PrimeChecker instance.\"\"\"\n        self._prime_checker = prime_checker\n\n    def get_value(self, n: int, x: Any, y: Any) -> Any:\n        \"\"\"Returns x if n is a prime number, and y otherwise.\n        Raises TypeError if n is not an integer.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(n, int):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n\n        if self._prime_checker.is_prime(n):\n            return x\n        else:\n            return y\n\n# file: src/main.py\nfrom src.prime_checker import PrimeChecker\nfrom src.x_or_y_service import XOrYService\n\ndef main():\n    \"\"\"Main entry point of the application.\n    Demonstrates the usage of XOrYService.\"\"\"\n    prime_checker = PrimeChecker()\n    x_or_y_service = XOrYService(prime_checker)\n\n    # Example 1: n is prime (7), returns x (34)\n    n1, x1, y1 = 7, 34, 12\n    result1 = x_or_y_service.get_value(n1, x1, y1)\n    print(f\"For n={n1}, x={x1}, y={y1}: Result = {result1} (Expected: 34)\")\n\n    # Example 2: n is not prime (15), returns y (5)\n    n2, x2, y2 = 15, 8, 5\n    result2 = x_or_y_service.get_value(n2, x2, y2)\n    print(f\"For n={n2}, x={x2}, y={y2}: Result = {result2} (Expected: 5)\")\n\n    # Example 3: n is prime (2), returns x (\"hello\")\n    n3, x3, y3 = 2, \"hello\", \"world\"\n    result3 = x_or_y_service.get_value(n3, x3, y3)\n    print(f\"For n={n3}, x={x3}, y={y3}: Result = {result3} (Expected: hello)\")\n\n    # Example 4: n is not prime (1), returns y (False)\n    n4, x4, y4 = 1, True, False\n    result4 = x_or_y_service.get_value(n4, x4, y4)\n    print(f\"For n={n4}, x={x4}, y={y4}: Result = {result4} (Expected: False)\")\n\n    # Example with invalid input type for n\n    try:\n        x_or_y_service.get_value(\"abc\", 10, 20)\n    except TypeError as e:\n        print(f\"Caught expected error: {e}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n# file: pyproject.toml\n[project]\nname = \"x-or-y-prime-checker\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"Determines primality of a number and returns one of two values.\"\nauthors = [\n    { name = \"Your Name\", email = \"your.email@example.com\" },\n]\nlicense = { text = \"MIT\" }\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.8\"\nkeywords = [\"prime\", \"math\", \"utility\"]\nclassifiers = [\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3\",\n    \"License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License\",\n    \"Operating System :: OS Independent\",\n]\n\n[project.urls]\nHomepage = \"https://github.com/yourusername/x-or-y-prime-checker\"\n\"Bug Tracker\" = \"https://github.com/yourusername/x-or-y-prime-checker/issues\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n# file: README.md\n# X-Or-Y Prime Checker\n\nThis project provides a Python application that determines if a given natural number `n` is prime. Based on its primality, it returns one of two provided values, `x` or `y`.\n\n## Features\n\n-   Efficient primality testing for integers.\n-   Returns a specified value (`x` or `y`) based on the primality test result.\n-   Robust input validation.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe system follows a simple layered architecture:\n-   **`PrimeChecker`**: Core logic for efficient prime number determination.\n-   **`XOrYService`**: Business logic that orchestrates the `PrimeChecker` and decides which value (`x` or `y`) to return.\n-   **`main.py`**: The application's entry point, demonstrating usage.\n\n## File Structure\n\n```\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 prime_checker.py\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 x_or_y_service.py\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 main.py\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 pyproject.toml\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 README.md\n```\n\n## Setup and Usage\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n-   Python 3.8+\n\n### Installation\n\n1.  Clone the repository:\n    ```bash\n    git clone https://github.com/yourusername/x-or-y-prime-checker.git\n    cd x-or-y-prime-checker\n    ```\n\n2.  (Optional) Create and activate a virtual environment:\n    ```bash\n    python -m venv venv\n    # On Windows\n    .\\venv\\Scripts\\activate\n    # On macOS/Linux\n    source venv/bin/activate\n    ```\n\n3.  Install the project (editable mode recommended for development):\n    ```bash\n    pip install -e .\n    ```\n\n### Running the Application\n\nTo run the main demonstration:\n\n```bash\npython src/main.py\n```\n\nThis will execute the examples defined in `main.py` and print their results to the console.\n\n## How to use the service programmatically:\n\n```python\nfrom src.prime_checker import PrimeChecker\nfrom src.x_or_y_service import XOrYService\n\n# Initialize the prime checker and service\nprime_checker = PrimeChecker()\nx_or_y_service = XOrYService(prime_checker)\n\n# Example usage\nnumber = 17\nvalue_if_prime = \"It's prime!\"\nvalue_if_not_prime = \"It's composite.\"\n\nresult = x_or_y_service.get_value(number, value_if_prime, value_if_not_prime)\nprint(f\"The number {number} is {result}\")\n\nnumber = 10\nresult = x_or_y_service.get_value(number, value_if_prime, value_if_not_prime)\nprint(f\"The number {number} is {result}\")\n\n# Handling invalid input\ntry:\n    x_or_y_service.get_value(3.14, \"Prime\", \"Not Prime\")\nexcept TypeError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n```\n\n## Development and Testing\n\nThe project structure supports unit testing, although test files are not included in this generated output.\nTo run tests (if they were present):\n```bash\n# Assuming you have pytest installed\npytest tests/\n```\n```"}
