classifiers = [\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3\",\n    \"License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License\",\n    \"Operating System :: OS Independent\",\n]\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n```\n\n```markdown\n# README.md\n# Roman Converter Mini\n\nA Python utility to convert positive integers (1-1000) into their lowercase Roman numeral string equivalent.\n\n## Installation\n\nThis is a standalone module. You can integrate it directly into your project by copying the `src/roman_converter` directory.\n\n## Usage\n\n```python\nfrom src.roman_converter.converter import int_to_mini_roman\n\n# Convert a number\nroman_numeral = int_to_mini_roman(42)\nprint(f\"42 in Roman numerals: {roman_numeral}\")\n\n# Handle invalid input\ntry:\n    int_to_mini_roman(0)\nexcept ValueError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n\ntry:\n    int_to_mini_roman(\"hello\")\nexcept ValueError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n```\n```"}
