{"task_id": "HumanEval/31", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\nclass PrimeCheckerService:\n    @staticmethod\n    def is_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Return true if a given number is prime, and false otherwise.\n        >>> PrimeCheckerService.is_prime(6)\n        False\n        >>> PrimeCheckerService.is_prime(101)\n        True\n        >>> PrimeCheckerService.is_prime(11)\n        True\n        >>> PrimeCheckerService.is_prime(13441)\n        True\n        >>> PrimeCheckerService.is_prime(61)\n        True\n        >>> PrimeCheckerService.is_prime(4)\n        False\n        >>> PrimeCheckerService.is_prime(1)\n        False\n        >>> PrimeCheckerService.is_prime(0)\n        False\n        >>> PrimeCheckerService.is_prime(-5)\n        False\n        >>> PrimeCheckerService.is_prime(2)\n        True\n        \"\"\"\n        if n <= 1:\n            return False\n        if n == 2:\n            return True\n        if n % 2 == 0:\n            return False\n        \n        # Check for divisibility from 3 up to sqrt(n) with a step of 2.\n        # Only odd numbers need to be checked after handling 2 and even numbers.\n        for i in range(3, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1, 2):\n            if n % i == 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/31", "solution": "```python\n# src/primality_checker/__init__.py\n\"\"\"\nInitializes the primality_checker package.\n\"\"\"\n\n# You might expose key functions directly here for easier import:\n# from .services import PrimalityService\n```\n```python\n# src/primality_checker/exceptions.py\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input to primality checking functions.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n```\n```python\n# src/primality_checker/services.py\nimport math\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\nclass PrimalityService:\n    \"\"\"\n    Service for determining if a given number is prime.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def is_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Return true if a given number is prime, and false otherwise.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(n, int):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input must be an integer.\")\n\n        if n <= 1:\n            return False\n        if n <= 3:\n            return True\n        if n % 2 == 0 or n % 3 == 0:\n            return False\n\n        i = 5\n        while i * i <= n:\n            if n % i == 0 or n % (i + 2) == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 6\n        return True\n```\n```python\n# pyproject.toml\n[project]\nname = \"primality_checker\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A utility library for efficient primality testing.\"\nauthors = [{ name = \"Your Name\", email = \"your.email@example.com\" }]\nrequires-python = \">=3.8\"\nlicense = { text = \"MIT\" }\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nkeywords = [\"prime\", \"primality\", \"math\", \"utility\"]\nclassifiers = [\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3\",\n    \"License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License\",\n    \"Operating System :: OS Independent\",\n    \"Development Status :: 3 - Alpha\",\n    \"Intended Audience :: Developers\",\n    \"Topic :: Software Development :: Libraries :: Python Modules\",\n    \"Topic :: Scientific/Engineering :: Mathematics\",\n]\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[tool.setuptools.packages.find]\nwhere = [\"src\"]\n```\n```python\n# README.md\n# Primality Checker\n\nA simple Python utility library for efficiently determining if a given integer is a prime number.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Efficient Primality Testing**: Implements an optimized algorithm (6k \u00b1 1 optimization) to check for primality.\n- **Type Safety**: Enforces integer input, raising a specific error for invalid types.\n- **Standalone Utility**: Designed as a self-contained function for easy integration into other applications.\n\n## Installation\n\nThis library can be installed directly from a local source.\n\n```bash\n# Example for local installation (from the root directory of the project)\npip install .\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n```python\nfrom primality_checker.services import PrimalityService\nfrom primality_checker.exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\n# Check if a number is prime\nprint(f\"Is 13 prime? {PrimalityService.is_prime(13)}\")\nprint(f\"Is 10 prime? {PrimalityService.is_prime(10)}\")\nprint(f\"Is 999983 prime? {PrimalityService.is_prime(999983)}\")\n\n# Handle invalid input\ntry:\n    PrimalityService.is_prime(6.5)\nexcept InvalidInputError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n```\n\n## Development\n\nTo set up the development environment:\n\n1. Clone the repository:\n   ```bash\n   # git clone https://github.com/your-username/primality-checker.git\n   # cd primality-checker\n   ```\n2. Install dependencies (if any):\n   ```bash\n   pip install -e .\n   ```\n\n## Contributing\n\nContributions are welcome!\n\n## License\n\nThis project is licensed under the MIT License.\n```\n```python\n# .gitignore\n# Byte-compiled / optimized / DLL files\n__pycache__/\n*.pyc\n*.pyd\n*.pyo\n*.egg-info/\n.pytest_cache/\n.coverage\nhtmlcov/\n.nox/\n.mypy_cache/\n.ruff_cache/\n\n# Distribution / packaging\n