{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "```python\nclass ListSorter:\n    @staticmethod\n    def sort_third(l: list) -> list:\n        \"\"\"Sorts elements at indices divisible by three in a list.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(l, list):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n        elements_at_third_indices = []\n        original_third_indices = []\n\n        for i, value in enumerate(l):\n            if i % 3 == 0:\n                elements_at_third_indices.append(value)\n                original_third_indices.append(i)\n\n        elements_at_third_indices.sort()\n\n        result_list = list(l)\n\n        for i, original_idx in enumerate(original_third_indices):\n            result_list[original_idx] = elements_at_third_indices[i]\n        \n        return result_list\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Any\n\ndef sort_third(l: List[Any]) -> List[Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the indices that are not divisible by three,\n    while its values at the indices that are divisible by three are equal\n    to the values of the corresponding indices of l, but sorted.\n\n    Args:\n        l: The input list of comparable elements.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new list with elements at indices divisible by three sorted.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If the input 'l' is not a list.\n        TypeError/ValueError: If elements within the list are not comparable during sorting.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(l, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    if not l:\n        return []\n\n    # Identify indices divisible by three and extract their values.\n    indices_to_sort = [i for i in range(len(l)) if i % 3 == 0]\n    values_to_sort = [l[i] for i in indices_to_sort]\n\n    # Sort the extracted values.\n    try:\n        values_to_sort.sort()\n    except TypeError as e:\n        raise TypeError(f\"Elements in the list are not comparable: {e}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise ValueError(f\"An unexpected error occurred during sorting: {e}\")\n\n    # Create a new list as a shallow copy of the original.\n    result_list = list(l)\n\n    # Place sorted values back into the new list at their original positions.\n    sorted_idx = 0\n    for i in indices_to_sort:\n        result_list[i] = values_to_sort[sorted_idx]\n        sorted_idx += 1\n\n    return result_list\n```"}
