{"task_id": "HumanEval/16", "solution": "```text\nsrc/string_utils/__init__.py\n```\n\n```python\n# Initializes the string_utils package.\n```\n\n```text\nsrc/string_utils/counter.py\n```\n\n```python\nclass DistinctCharacterCounter:\n    \"\"\"Provides methods to count distinct characters in strings.\"\"\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def count_distinct_characters(input_string: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the number of unique characters in the input string, ignoring case.\n        Raises TypeError if the input is not a string.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(input_string, str):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n        \n        # Convert the string to lowercase for case-insensitive comparison.\n        lower_string = input_string.lower()\n        \n        # Use a set to efficiently store and count unique characters.\n        distinct_chars = set(lower_string)\n            \n        return len(distinct_chars)\n\n```\n\n```text\nsrc/main.py\n```\n\n```python\nfrom src.string_utils.counter import DistinctCharacterCounter\n\ndef main():\n    \"\"\"Demonstrates the usage of the DistinctCharacterCounter.\"\"\"\n    test_strings = [\n        \"xyzXYZ\",\n        \"Jerry\",\n        \"Hello World\",\n        \"Python is fun!\",\n        \"\",\n        \"aaaaa\",\n        \"123!@#ABCabc\",\n        \"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog\"\n    ]\n\n    print(\"--- Distinct Character Counter Demo ---\")\n    for s in test_strings:\n        try:\n            count = DistinctCharacterCounter.count_distinct_characters(s)\n            print(f\"String: '{s}' -> Distinct Characters: {count}\")\n        except TypeError as e:\n            print(f\"Error processing '{s}': {e}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```\n\n```text\npyproject.toml\n```\n\n```toml\n[project]\nname = \"string-utils\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A utility package for string operations, including counting distinct characters.\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.8\"\nkeywords = [\"string\", \"utility\", \"unique characters\", \"case-insensitive\"]\nclassifiers = [\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3\",\n    \"License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License\",\n    \"Operating System :: OS Independent\",\n]\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n```\n\n```text\nREADME.md\n```\n\n```markdown\n# String Utilities\n\nThis project provides a simple Python utility to count the number of distinct characters within a given string, disregarding character casing.\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 string_utils/\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py         # Initializes the string_utils package.\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 counter.py          # Contains the core logic for counting distinct characters.\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 main.py                 # Example usage of the distinct character counter.\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 pyproject.toml              # Project metadata and build configuration.\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 README.md                   # Project description and usage instructions.\n```\n\n## Core Functionality\n\nThe main functionality is encapsulated in the `DistinctCharacterCounter` class, specifically its `count_distinct_characters` static method.\n\n### `DistinctCharacterCounter.count_distinct_characters(input_string: str) -> int`\n\n*   **Purpose:** Calculates the number of unique characters in the `input_string`, treating uppercase and lowercase versions of the same letter as identical.\n*   **Parameters:**\n    *   `input_string` (str): The string to analyze.\n*   **Returns:**\n    *   `int`: The count of distinct characters.\n*   **Raises:**\n    *   `TypeError`: If `input_string` is not a string.\n\n## Installation\n\n1.  **Clone the repository:**\n    ```bash\n    git clone <repository_url> # Replace with your repository URL\n    cd string-utils\n    ```\n2.  **(Optional) Create a virtual environment:**\n    ```bash\n    python -m venv .venv\n    source .venv/bin/activate\n    ```\n3.  **Install the package:**\n    ```bash\n    pip install .\n    ```\n\n## Usage\n\nYou can use the `count_distinct_characters` method directly in your Python code:\n\n```python\nfrom string_utils.counter import DistinctCharacterCounter\n\n# Example 1: Mixed case string\ns1 = \"Hello World!\"\ncount1 = DistinctCharacterCounter.count_distinct_characters(s1)\nprint(f\"The string '{s1}' has {count1} distinct characters.\") # Output: 10 (h, e, l, o,  , w, r, d, !)\n\n# Example 2: String with repeated characters and varying case\ns2 = \"Mississippi\"\ncount2 = DistinctCharacterCounter.count_distinct_characters(s2)\nprint(f\"The string '{s2}' has {count2} distinct characters.\") # Output: 4 (m, i, s, p)\n\n# Example 3: Empty string\ns3 = \"\"\ncount3 = DistinctCharacterCounter.count_distinct_characters(s3)\nprint(f\"The string '{s3}' has {count3} distinct characters.\") # Output: 0\n\n# Example 4: Non-string input (will raise TypeError)\ntry:\n    DistinctCharacterCounter.count_distinct_characters(123)\nexcept TypeError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n```\n\n### Running the Example Script\n\nAn example script (`src/main.py`) is provided to demonstrate the utility with various test cases.\n\n```bash\npython src/main.py\n```\n\n## Development and Testing\n\nThe project includes unit tests to ensure correctness and performance. (Note: unit tests are not included in this generated output as per specific instructions but are part of the overall design.)\n\n```bash\n# To run tests (if tests were generated and setup)\n# python -m unittest discover tests\n```\n```"}
